	"notes": "This is a classic two-column blog: a day-by-day list of posts on the left and a short 'Highlights' list floating beside it on the right, both fixed widths sitting inside a 960px column that centres itself on the page — so a wide monitor just adds space on the sides, it never makes the columns bigger. What makes this one different from the other blogs in this batch is HOW the two columns are built: plain CSS float, the technique the web used for multi-column pages before flexbox and grid existed. It still works exactly the way it always has — the text wraps around the floated box until the box ends. Below about 800px the float layout gives up and the highlights list moves down to the very bottom of the page, well after the last post, rather than appearing near the top.",
